{"step_index":128,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:18:09Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-26T00:48:09+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-26T00:48:09+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/mcp/nexlev/get_similar_channels.json`\nTotal Lines: 1\nTotal Bytes: 1207\nShowing lines 1 to 1\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: {\"name\":\"get_similar_channels\",\"description\":\"Use this when you have a specific YouTube channel and want to find its competitors or similar channels. Requires a channel ID (use channel_resolver first if you have a URL). Always set async=true — this returns a jobId, then poll `get_similar_channels_status` with that jobId every 5 seconds until status is \\\"completed\\\" or \\\"failed\\\" (up to 150 seconds). Use level=1 for quick results, level=3 for thorough deep search. Do NOT use this for topic-based niche discovery — use search_niche_finder_channels instead.\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"async\":{\"default\":true,\"description\":\"ALWAYS set this to true. Returns a jobId immediately for polling via get_similar_channels_status instead of waiting synchronously.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"channelId\":{\"description\":\"YouTube Channel ID to find similar channels for\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"channelType\":{\"default\":\"all\",\"description\":\"Type of channel content to search for\",\"enum\":[\"all\",\"short\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"level\":{\"default\":1,\"description\":\"Search depth level (1: quick, 2: moderate, 3: in-depth)\",\"maximum\":3,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"channelId\"],\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":129,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:18:09Z","content":"Good — NexLev is authenticated and working. The `get_channel_analytics` is just rate-limited (5/day used). Let me now use the tools with higher limits. First, let me get the channel info via `youtube_channel_about` (50/day limit) and then the channel videos.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import asyncio\\nimport sys\\nimport json\\nfrom mcp.client.stdio import stdio_client, StdioServerParameters\\nfrom mcp.client.session import ClientSession\\n\\nasync def call_tool(tool_name, arguments):\\n    server_params = StdioServerParameters(\\n        command=\\\"npx.cmd\\\",\\n        args=[\\\"-y\\\", \\\"mcp-remote\\\", \\\"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\\\"],\\n    )\\n\\n    async with stdio_client(server_params) as (read, write):\\n        async with ClientSession(read, write) as session:\\n            await session.initialize()\\n            result = await session.call_tool(tool_name, arguments)\\n            return result\\n\\nasync def main():\\n    tool_name = sys.argv[1]\\n    args_json = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else \\\"{}\\\"\\n    arguments = json.loads(args_json)\\n    \\n    result = await call_tool(tool_name, arguments)\\n    \\n    # Print just the text content\\n    for content in result.content:\\n        print(content.text)\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    asyncio.run(main())\\n\"","Description":"\"Reusable NexLev MCP caller — pass tool name and JSON args as CLI arguments\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\nexlev_call.py\"","toolAction":"\"Writing reusable NexLev caller\"","toolSummary":"\"NexLev MCP caller script\""}}]}
